                <h3><b>Managing Change During Telemedicine Adoption</b></h3>
                <p>
                    Telemedicine introduces new digital workflows for healthcare professionals, administrators, and patients. Change management helps users transition confidently to remote healthcare services.
                </p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Communicate the New Workflow: Clearly explain how remote consultations will work and what users should expect.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Engage Providers and Staff: Involve healthcare professionals and support teams in workflow design and testing.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Train Users: Provide simple guidance for consultation access, scheduling, communication, and support.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Pilot Before Full Rollout: Use a controlled pilot to identify workflow and usability issues before wider deployment.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Continuous Support: Monitor user feedback and resolve operational issues after launch.
